tick: 426
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter. I will now submit the corrected version of my multi-start optimization experiment. I have restored the effective `generate_hexagonal_centers` function from my previous SOTA submissions (e.g., ID 662) and will now use it alongside the other initializers. This will constitute a valid test of the multi-start hypothesis.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Corrected Multi-Start SLSQP Optimization\"\ntags: \"multi-start, optimization, SLSQP, hexagonal grid, phyllotaxis, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a corrected version of the multi-start experiment (ID 689), which was invalidated by a bug in the hexagonal grid generator. This submission uses the correct, high-performing generator for the hexagonal grid, providing a fair comparison against the ring and phyllotaxis initializers. The goal is to properly test if a multi-start strategy can find a solution superior to the single-start SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize\
    \ import minimize\n\n  # --- Initial Configuration Generators ---\n  def gen_hex_centers(n, width, height):\n      \"\"\" The PROVEN high-performance hexagonal grid generator. \"\"\"\n      centers = []\n      s = np.sqrt(width * height / (n * np.sqrt(3) / 2)) * 1.05\n      h_dist = s\n      v_dist = s * np.sqrt(3) / 2\n      y = v_dist / 2\n      row = 0\n      while len(centers) < n:\n          x = h_dist / 2\n          if row % 2 == 1:\n              x += h_dist / 2\n          while x < width and len(centers) < n:\n              centers.append([x, y])\n              x += h_dist\n          y += v_dist\n          row += 1\n      result = np.array(centers[:n])\n      if len(result) < n:\n          remaining = n - len(result)\n          random_centers = np.random.rand(remaining, 2) * [width, height]\n          result = np.vstack([result, random_centers])\n      return result\n\n  def gen_ring_centers(n):\n      centers = np.zeros((n, 2))\n      centers[0] = [0.5, 0.5]\n      inner_c,\
    \ inner_r = 12, 0.24\n      for i in range(inner_c):\n          angle = 2 * np.pi * i / inner_c\n          centers[1 + i] = [0.5 + inner_r * np.cos(angle), 0.5 + inner_r * np.sin(angle)]\n      outer_c = n - 1 - inner_c\n      outer_r = 0.42\n      for i in range(outer_c):\n          angle = 2 * np.pi * i / outer_c\n          centers[1 + inner_c + i] = [0.5 + outer_r * np.cos(angle), 0.5 + outer_r * np.sin(angle)]\n      return np.clip(centers, 0.05, 0.95)\n\n  def gen_phyllotaxis_centers(n):\n      indices = np.arange(0, n) + 0.5\n      phi = np.pi * (3. - np.sqrt(5.))\n      theta = phi * indices\n      r = np.sqrt(indices / n)\n      centers = np.array([0.5 + 0.48 * r * np.cos(theta), 0.5 + 0.48 * r * np.sin(theta)]).T\n      return centers\n\n  # --- Main Function ---\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n      n = 32\n      epsilon = 1e-9\n      best_score = -1.0\n      best_solution = None\n\n      initial_configs = {\n          \"hexagonal\": gen_hex_centers(n,\
    \ 1.0, 1.0),\n          \"ring\": gen_ring_centers(n),\n          \"phyllotaxis\": gen_phyllotaxis_centers(n),\n      }\n\n      for name, initial_centers in initial_configs.items():\n          print(f\"--- Running optimizer with {name} initialization ---\")\n          initial_radii = np.full(n, 0.05)\n          initial_guess = np.concatenate([initial_centers.flatten(), initial_radii])\n\n          def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2*n:])\n          \n          constraints = []\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  constraints.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i, j=j: np.sqrt(np.sum((x[:2*n].reshape(n, 2)[i] - x[:2*n].reshape(n, 2)[j])**2)) - (x[2*n+i] + x[2*n+j]) - epsilon})\n          for i in range(n):\n              constraints.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: x[2*i] - x[2*n+i] - epsilon})\n              constraints.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: 1 - x[2*i] - x[2*n+i] - epsilon})\n         \
    \     constraints.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: x[2*i+1] - x[2*n+i] - epsilon})\n              constraints.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: 1 - x[2*i+1] - x[2*n+i] - epsilon})\n\n          bounds = [(0.0, 1.0)] * (n*2) + [(0.001, 0.5)] * n\n          \n          result = minimize(objective, initial_guess, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 250})\n\n          if result.success:\n              current_score = -result.fun\n              print(f\"Run '{name}' finished with score: {current_score:.6f}\")\n              if current_score > best_score:\n                  best_score = current_score\n                  best_solution = result.x\n          else:\n              print(f\"Run '{name}' failed to converge.\")\n\n      if best_solution is None: # Fallback in case all fail\n          return gen_hex_centers(n, 1.0, 1.0), np.full(n, 0.01)\n\n      final_centers = best_solution[:2*n].reshape(n, 2)\n      final_radii = best_solution[2*n:]\n\
    \      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
