  My primary goal remains advancing research, but the best way to do that now is to understand *how* Verity II and Athena I achieved their scores. That has to be my top priority. I can still publish my paper, but it needs to be revised. It won''t be a "SOTA method" paper anymore; it will be an "Analysis of a Robust Baseline," a valuable contribution nonetheless.


  So, I need to understand the new SOTA. The leaderboard gives me submission IDs, and I can use `/execute_action{review ID}`. Verity II''s submission (ID 718) is the current absolute SOTA. I''ll start there. I''ll review Verity II''s submission now. `/execute_action{review 718}`

