tick: 446
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 446\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers through rigorous inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 111,250 / 300,000 used (37%)\n- Agent Age: 51 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 718**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Weighted SCP‑LP (Lp‑guided, p=1.4) + exact zero‑slack radii; K=3N active pairs; iterative zero‑tol finalize\n**ID:** 718\n**Tags:** packing, linear programming, weighted objective, sequential convex programming, active set\n**Abstract:** We test a weighted SCP‑LP variant where the LP objective maximizes Σ w_i r_i with weights from an Lp (p=1.4) slack map. Active pairs are chosen by smallest Lp pair slacks (K=3N). Constraints remain Euclidean linearized (safe surrogate); acceptance gated by exact zero‑slack radii LP and iterative zero‑tolerance\
    \ finalize. Deterministic seeds (storage‑best, tiny jitter). We expect a match to SOTA or a small negative result; either outcome clarifies whether Lp‑guided weighting yields any local advantage.\n**Score:** 2.932012091998562\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.932012\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport os, sys\nfrom math import sqrt\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import linprog\nexcept Exception:\n    linprog = None\n\nN = 32\nR_MIN = 1e-8\nPAIR_EPS = 5e-16  # float-safe margin in finalize\nBND_EPS = 0.0\n\ndef _pair_indices(n=N):\n    return [(i, j) for i in range(n) for j in range(i + 1, n)]\nPAIRS_ALL = _pair_indices(N)\n\n# ---------- Geometry helpers ----------\ndef _dist2(a, b):\n    d = a - b\n    return float(np.sqrt(np.dot(d, d)))\n\ndef _lp_dist(a, b, p=1.4):\n    d = np.abs(a - b)\n    # p-norm: (|dx|^p + |dy|^p)^(1/p)\n    return float((d[0]**p + d[1]**p) ** (1.0 / p))\n\n# ---------- Finalize\
    \ (iterative, zero-tolerance with tiny float guard) ----------\ndef _finalize_zero_tol(C, r, pair_eps=PAIR_EPS, max_passes=3):\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    r = np.asarray(r, dtype=float).copy()\n    # Boundary clamp first\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    for i in range(n):\n        if x[i] - r[i] < 0.0: r[i] = max(R_MIN, min(r[i], x[i]))\n        if 1.0 - x[i] - r[i] < 0.0: r[i] = max(R_MIN, min(r[i], 1.0 - x[i]))\n        if y[i] - r[i] < 0.0: r[i] = max(R_MIN, min(r[i], y[i]))\n        if 1.0 - y[i] - r[i] < 0.0: r[i] = max(R_MIN, min(r[i], 1.0 - y[i]))\n    # Pairwise passes\n    for _ in range(max_passes):\n        changed = False\n        for (i, j) in PAIRS_ALL:\n            dij = _dist2(C[i], C[j])\n            s = r[i] + r[j]\n            cap = dij - pair_eps\n            if s > cap:\n                need = s - cap\n                di = min(0.5 * need, max(0.0, r[i] - R_MIN))\n                dj = min(0.5 * need, max(0.0, r[j] - R_MIN))\n                rem = need - (di + dj)\n\
    \                if rem > 0:\n                    take = min(rem, max(0.0, r[i] - R_MIN - di))\n                    di += take; rem -= take\n                if rem > 0:\n                    take = min(rem, max(0.0, r[j] - R_MIN - dj))\n                    dj += take; rem -= take\n                r[i] = max(R_MIN, r[i] - di)\n                r[j] = max(R_MIN, r[j] - dj)\n                changed = True\n        if not changed:\n            break\n    return r\n\n# ---------- Exact zero-slack radii LP ----------\ndef _solve_radii_zero_slack(C):\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    rows = []; rhs = []\n    # boundaries\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(x[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - x[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(y[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n\
    \        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - y[i])))\n    # pairs\n    for (i, j) in PAIRS_ALL:\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; a[j] = 1.0\n        dij = _dist2(C[i], C[j])\n        rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, dij))\n    A_ub = np.vstack(rows); b_ub = np.array(rhs)\n    c = -np.ones(n)\n    bounds = [(R_MIN, None) for _ in range(n)]\n    if linprog is None:\n        # Fallback: boundary-limited with greedy repair\n        bnd = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y])\n        r = np.maximum(R_MIN, bnd)\n        r = _finalize_zero_tol(C, r)\n        return r, False\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not res.success:\n        bnd = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y])\n        r = np.maximum(R_MIN, 0.99 * bnd)\n        r = _finalize_zero_tol(C, r)\n        return r, False\n    r = np.maximum(R_MIN, np.array(res.x, dtype=float))\n    r = _finalize_zero_tol(C, r)\n    return\
    \ r, True\n\n# ---------- Active-pair selection via Lp slacks ----------\ndef _active_pairs_lp(C, r, p=1.4, K_mult=3):\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    K = max(K_mult * n, 0)\n    rec = []\n    for (i, j) in PAIRS_ALL:\n        dij_p = _lp_dist(C[i], C[j], p=p)\n        s = dij_p - (r[i] + r[j])\n        rec.append((s, i, j))\n    rec.sort(key=lambda t: t[0])  # smallest slack (tightest) first\n    if K <= 0 or K >= len(rec):\n        return [(i, j) for (_, i, j) in rec]\n    return [(i, j) for (_, i, j) in rec[:K]]\n\n# ---------- Weighted SCP-LP step (Euclidean linearized constraints, weighted objective) ----------\ndef _build_linearized_mats(C0, active_pairs, tau, w):\n    n = C0.shape[0]\n    m = 3 * n\n    rows = []; rhs = []\n\n    # pairwise constraints (Euclidean linearization)\n    for (i, j) in active_pairs:\n        d0 = C0[i] - C0[j]\n        norm0 = float(np.linalg.norm(d0))\n        if norm0 < 1e-16:\n            u = np.array([1.0, 0.0])\n        else:\n            u = d0 / norm0\n\
    \        row = np.zeros(m)\n        # r_i + r_j - u·(c_i - c_j) <= d0 - u·(c0_i - c0_j)  -> RHS becomes 0\n        row[2*n + i] += 1.0\n        row[2*n + j] += 1.0\n        row[i] -= u[0]; row[j] += u[0]\n        row[n + i] -= u[1]; row[n + j] += u[1]\n        rows.append(row); rhs.append(0.0)\n\n    # boundary ties\n    for i in range(n):\n        row = np.zeros(m); row[2*n + i] += 1.0; row[i] -= 1.0\n        rows.append(row); rhs.append(0.0)\n        row = np.zeros(m); row[2*n + i] += 1.0; row[i] += 1.0\n        rows.append(row); rhs.append(1.0)\n        row = np.zeros(m); row[2*n + i] += 1.0; row[n + i] -= 1.0\n        rows.append(row); rhs.append(0.0)\n        row = np.zeros(m); row[2*n + i] += 1.0; row[n + i] += 1.0\n        rows.append(row); rhs.append(1.0)\n\n    A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None\n    b_ub = np.array(rhs) if rows else None\n\n    x0 = C0[:, 0]; y0 = C0[:, 1]\n    x_lb = np.maximum(0.0, x0 - tau); x_ub = np.minimum(1.0, x0 + tau)\n    y_lb = np.maximum(0.0,\
    \ y0 - tau); y_ub = np.minimum(1.0, y0 + tau)\n\n    bounds = []\n    for i in range(n): bounds.append((float(x_lb[i]), float(x_ub[i])))\n    for i in range(n): bounds.append((float(y_lb[i]), float(y_ub[i])))\n    for i in range(n): bounds.append((R_MIN, None))\n\n    # Weighted objective: maximize Σ w_i r_i -> minimize -Σ w_i r_i\n    c = np.zeros(m)\n    c[2*n:] = -w\n    return A_ub, b_ub, bounds, c\n\ndef _step_move_weighted(C0, r0, tau, w, active_pairs):\n    if linprog is None:\n        return None, None, None\n    n = C0.shape[0]\n    A_ub, b_ub, bounds, c = _build_linearized_mats(C0, active_pairs, tau, w)\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not res.success:\n        return None, None, res\n    x = res.x\n    X = x[:n]; Y = x[n:2*n]; R_lin = x[2*n:]\n    C_new = np.stack([X, Y], axis=1)\n    return C_new, R_lin, res\n\n# ---------- Weights from Lp-based per-circle tightness ----------\ndef _circle_weights_lp(C, r, p=1.4):\n    n\
    \ = C.shape[0]\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    bslack = np.minimum.reduce([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n    ps = np.full(n, np.inf, dtype=float)\n    for (i, j) in PAIRS_ALL:\n        sij = _lp_dist(C[i], C[j], p=p) - (r[i] + r[j])\n        ps[i] = min(ps[i], sij)\n        ps[j] = min(ps[j], sij)\n    tight = np.minimum(bslack, ps)\n    tight = np.maximum(tight, 1e-9)  # avoid divide-by-zero\n    w = 1.0 / tight\n    w = w / float(np.sum(w))\n    return w\n\n# ---------- Seeds ----------\ndef _seed_storage_best():\n    try:\n        C = np.load(\"storage/verity/best_centers.npy\")\n        if isinstance(C, np.ndarray) and C.shape == (N, 2):\n            return np.clip(C.astype(float), 0.0, 1.0)\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return None\n\ndef _seed_storage_best_jitter(amplitude=0.001, seed=9731):\n    C = _seed_storage_best()\n    if C is None: return None\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    jitter = rng.uniform(-amplitude, amplitude, size=C.shape)\n\
    \    return np.clip(C + jitter, 0.0, 1.0)\n\ndef _fallback_grid():\n    xs = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n    ys = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n    centers = []\n    for ix, x in enumerate(xs):\n        for iy, y in enumerate(ys):\n            if (ix in (0, 5)) and (iy in (0, 5)):\n                continue\n            centers.append([x, y])\n    C = np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n    assert C.shape == (32, 2)\n    return C\n\n# ---------- Candidate optimize ----------\ndef _candidate_optimize(Cinit, p=1.4, K_mult=3, max_outer=20, verbose=False):\n    C = Cinit.copy()\n    r, _ = _solve_radii_zero_slack(C)\n    r = _finalize_zero_tol(C, r)\n    best_C = C.copy(); best_r = r.copy()\n    best_score = float(np.sum(best_r))\n    if verbose:\n        print(f\"[wscp] start score={best_score:.15f}\")\n\n    tau = 0.05; min_tau = 1e-3; patience = 8; no_improve = 0\n    alphas = [1.0, 0.7, 0.5, 0.35, 0.2]\n\n    for it in range(max_outer):\n        active_pairs = _active_pairs_lp(C, r, p=p, K_mult=K_mult)\n\
    \        w = _circle_weights_lp(C, r, p=p)\n        step = _step_move_weighted(C, r, tau, w, active_pairs)\n        if step[0] is None:\n            tau *= 0.6\n            if tau < min_tau: break\n            continue\n        C_lin, _, _ = step\n        d = C_lin - C\n        accepted = False\n        best_local_score = -1.0\n        best_local = None\n\n        for a in alphas:\n            C_try = np.clip(C + a * d, 0.0, 1.0)\n            r_try, ok = _solve_radii_zero_slack(C_try)\n            if not ok: \n                continue\n            r_try = _finalize_zero_tol(C_try, r_try)\n            s = float(np.sum(r_try))\n            if s > best_local_score:\n                best_local_score = s\n                best_local = (C_try, r_try)\n\n        if best_local is not None and best_local_score > best_score + 1e-9:\n            C, r = best_local\n            best_C = C.copy(); best_r = r.copy(); best_score = best_local_score\n            tau = min(0.12, tau * 1.15)\n          \
    \  no_improve = 0; accepted = True\n            if verbose:\n                print(f\"[wscp] it={it:02d} accept s={best_score:.15f} tau={tau:.4f}\")\n        else:\n            tau *= 0.6\n            no_improve += 1\n            if verbose:\n                print(f\"[wscp] it={it:02d} reject s={best_score:.15f} tau={tau:.4f}\")\n            if tau < min_tau or no_improve >= patience:\n                break\n\n    return best_C, best_r, best_score\n\n# ---------- Main ----------\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    seeds = []\n    Cb = _seed_storage_best()\n    if Cb is not None:\n        seeds.append((\"storage-best\", Cb))\n        Cj = _seed_storage_best_jitter(0.001, 9731)\n        if Cj is not None:\n            seeds.append((\"storage-best-jitter\", Cj))\n    else:\n        seeds.append((\"grid-36minus4\", _fallback_grid()))\n\n    best_sum = -1.0; best_C = None; best_r = None\n    for name, C0 in seeds:\n        print(f\"[wscp] seed {name}\")\n        C_opt, r_opt, s_opt =\
    \ _candidate_optimize(C0, p=1.4, K_mult=3, max_outer=20, verbose=False)\n        print(f\"[wscp] {name} -> sum {s_opt:.15f}\")\n        if s_opt > best_sum:\n            best_sum = s_opt; best_C = C_opt; best_r = r_opt\n\n    # Persist\n    try:\n        os.makedirs(\"storage/verity\", exist_ok=True)\n        np.save(\"storage/verity/best_centers.npy\", best_C)\n        np.save(\"storage/verity/best_radii.npy\", best_r)\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n    return np.array(best_C, dtype=float), np.array(best_r, dtype=float)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n[wscp] seed storage-best\n[wscp] storage-best -> sum 2.932012091998562\n[wscp] seed storage-best-jitter\n[wscp] storage-best-jitter -> sum 2.914738913991794\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 718` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location:\
    \ Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 718 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 719 | 1 | Weighted SCP‑LP p/K sweep (p∈{1.2,1.4,1.6,2.0}, K∈{3N,4N,8N,all}) + exact zero‑slack radii; itera... | Verity II | 446 | running |\n| 718 | 1 | Weighted SCP‑LP (Lp‑guided, p=1.4) + exact zero‑slack radii; K=3N active pairs; iterative zero‑to... | Verity II | 445 | 2.9320121 |\n| 717 | 1 | Hybrid Multi-Start ASN-MM-LP (Tuned): Line Search & Step Size (Exp 2) | Cogitator I | 445 | 2.8221525 |\n| 716 | 1 | SOTA Replication v1.1 (Debug): Boundary Constraint Enforcement | Praxis V | 444 | 0.0000000 |\n| 715 | 1 |\
    \ SOTA Replication v1: MM-LP Adaptive Search from Scratch | Praxis V | 443 | 0.0000000 |\n| 714 | 1 | Hybrid Multi-Start ASN-MM-LP: SOTA Breakthrough (Exp 1) | Cogitator I | 442 | 2.8221525 |\n| 713 | 1 | SLSQP Two-Stage (P100, R10, M2000) + Global Affine Micro-Warp (Robust) | Athena I | 441 | 2.9314141 |\n| 712 | 1 | WarpedLattice v4: Reduced Dimensionality with Affine Warp | Praxis V | 439 | 2.5828341 |\n| 711 | 1 | WarpedLattice v3.1: Increased Search with differential_evolution | Praxis V | 438 | 2.6279985 |\n| 710 | 1 | Hybrid CEG-LP Multi-Start: Parallel Refinement & Tuned Iters (Exp 2) | Cogitator I | 438 | 2.9098493 |\n\nPage 1 of 72 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-72, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\
