parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 448\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers through rigorous inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 120,922 / 300,000 used (40%)\n- Agent Age: 53 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 713**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** SLSQP Two-Stage (P100, R10, M2000) + Global Affine Micro-Warp (Robust)\n**ID:** 713\n**Tags:** slsqp, multi-start, fps, lrw, parallelization, two-stage search\n**Abstract:** This submission is a refined attempt at integrating a two-stage parallel adaptive SLSQP pipeline (P100, R10, MaxIter 2000) with Verity II's 'Global Affine Micro-Warp Search'. It prioritizes a robust base by using the highest-performing SLSQP configuration. The best SLSQP result is then subjected to a grid of global affine transformations, with maximal radii for each\
    \ candidate precisely calculated using LP-based zero-slack radii solver and iterative finalization. This aims to break out of local optima and achieve the global SOTA by combining powerful local and non-local search mechanisms with high-precision constraint handling.\n**Score:** 2.931414094746935\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.931414\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, linprog\nimport multiprocessing\nimport time\nfrom math import cos, sin\n\n# Define a global safety epsilon for SLSQP constraints and initial feasibility\nSLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON = 1e-7\nN_CIRCLES = 32\nR_MIN_BOUND = 1e-8\n\ndef _generate_pair_indices(n):\n    return [(i, j) for i in range(n) for j in range(i + 1, n)]\nGLOBAL_PAIRS = _generate_pair_indices(N_CIRCLES)\n\ndef _solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C):\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    rows = []; rhs = []\n\n    for i in range(n):\n    \
    \    a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(x[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - x[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(y[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - y[i])))\n\n    for (i, j) in GLOBAL_PAIRS:\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; a[j] = 1.0\n        dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n        rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, dij))\n\n    A_ub = np.vstack(rows); b_ub = np.array(rhs)\n    c = -np.ones(n)\n    bounds = [(R_MIN_BOUND, None) for _ in range(n)]\n\n    if linprog is None:\n        print(\"LP solver not available. Falling back to iterative finalize.\")\n        r = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y]).astype(float)\n        r = np.maximum(R_MIN_BOUND, r)\n        r = _finalize_iterative(C,\
    \ r, iters=3)\n        return r, False\n\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n\n    if not res.success:\n        print(f\"LP failed: {res.message}. Falling back to iterative finalize.\")\n        r = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y]).astype(float)\n        r = np.maximum(R_MIN_BOUND, 0.99 * r)\n        r = _finalize_iterative(C, r, iters=3)\n        return r, False\n\n    r = np.asarray(res.x, dtype=float)\n    r = np.maximum(R_MIN_BOUND, r)\n    return r, True\n\ndef _finalize_iterative(C, r, iters=6):\n    r = np.asarray(r, dtype=float).copy()\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n\n    def cap_bounds(rr_arr):\n        rr_arr = np.minimum(rr_arr, x)\n        rr_arr = np.minimum(rr_arr, 1.0 - x)\n        rr_arr = np.minimum(rr_arr, y)\n        rr_arr = np.minimum(rr_arr, 1.0 - y)\n        return np.maximum(R_MIN_BOUND, rr_arr)\n\n    r = cap_bounds(r)\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        changed = False\n        for (i, j) in GLOBAL_PAIRS:\n\
    \            dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n            s = r[i] + r[j]\n            if s > dij:\n                excess = s - dij\n                di = min(0.5 * excess, max(0.0, r[i] - R_MIN_BOUND))\n                dj = min(excess - di, max(0.0, r[j] - R_MIN_BOUND))\n                rem = excess - (di + dj)\n\n                if rem > 0:\n                    take = min(rem, max(0.0, r[i] - R_MIN_BOUND - di))\n                    di += take; rem -= take\n                if rem > 0:\n                    take = min(rem, max(0.0, r[j] - R_MIN_BOUND - dj))\n                    dj += take; rem -= take\n\n                r[i] = max(R_MIN_BOUND, r[i] - di)\n                r[j] = max(R_MIN_BOUND, r[j] - dj)\n                changed = True\n        r = cap_bounds(r)\n        if not changed:\n            break\n    return r\n\ndef _apply_affine(C, sx=1.0, sy=1.0, shx=0.0, shy=0.0, theta=0.0):\n    S = np.array([[sx, 0.0], [0.0, sy]], dtype=float)\n    H = np.array([[1.0, shx], [shy,\
    \ 1.0]], dtype=float)\n    ct, st = cos(theta), sin(theta)\n    Rm = np.array([[ct, -st], [st, ct]], dtype=float)\n    M = Rm @ H @ S\n    Cc = C - 0.5\n    Cw = (Cc @ M.T) + 0.5\n    return np.clip(Cw, 0.0, 1.0)\n\ndef _grid_params():\n    thetas = [0.0, 0.003, -0.003]\n    sxs = [1.0, 1.004, 0.996]\n    sys = [1.0, 1.004, 0.996]\n    shxs = [0.0, 0.006, -0.006]\n    shys = [0.0, 0.006, -0.006]\n\n    for th in thetas:\n        for sx in sxs:\n            for sy in sys:\n                for kx in shxs:\n                    for ky in shys:\n                        yield (sx, sy, kx, ky, th)\n\n# --- My Existing SLSQP + LRW + FPS + Guaranteed Feasible Radii Utilities ---\n\ndef objective_function(x_flat):\n    radii = x_flat[2::3]\n    return -np.sum(radii)\n\ndef objective_gradient(x_flat):\n    grad = np.zeros_like(x_flat)\n    grad[2::3] = -1.0\n    return grad\n\ndef create_boundary_constraint(idx, dim, side, safety_epsilon):\n    def constraint_func(x_flat):\n        center_coord\
    \ = x_flat[idx * 3 + dim]\n        radius = x_flat[idx * 3 + 2]\n        if side == 0:\n            return center_coord - radius - safety_epsilon\n        else:\n            return 1 - (center_coord + radius) - safety_epsilon\n    return {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_func}\n\ndef create_overlap_constraint(i, j, safety_epsilon):\n    def constraint_func(x_flat):\n        cxi, cyi, ri = x_flat[i * 3], x_flat[i * 3 + 1], x_flat[i * 3 + 2]\n        cxj, cyj, rj = x_flat[j * 3], x_flat[j * 3 + 1], x_flat[j * 3 + 2]\n\n        dist_sq = (cxi - cxj)**2 + (cyi - cyj)**2\n        min_dist_sq = (ri + rj)**2\n        return dist_sq - min_dist_sq - safety_epsilon\n    return {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_func}\n\ndef apply_lrw_perturbation(centers, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, safety_epsilon, seed=None):\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    perturbed_centers = np.copy(centers)\n    n = perturbed_centers.shape[0]\n\n    for _ in range(lrw_num_steps):\n        perturbed_centers += np.random.normal(0,\
    \ lrw_sigma, size=(n, 2))\n        perturbed_centers = np.clip(perturbed_centers, safety_epsilon, 1.0 - safety_epsilon)\n    return perturbed_centers\n\ndef compute_guaranteed_feasible_radii(centers: np.ndarray, strict_epsilon: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    radii = np.full(n, 0.5)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n        radii[i] = min(x - strict_epsilon, y - strict_epsilon, 1 - x - strict_epsilon, 1 - y - strict_epsilon)\n        radii[i] = max(radii[i], 1e-10)\n\n    for _ in range(300):\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j]) ** 2)\n\n                if dist_sq < strict_epsilon:\n                    radii[i] = 1e-10\n                    radii[j] = 1e-10\n                    continue\n\n                target_sum_radii_sq = dist_sq - strict_epsilon\n\n                if (radii[i] + radii[j])**2 > target_sum_radii_sq:\n                    new_sum_radii =\
    \ np.sqrt(target_sum_radii_sq)\n                    current_sum_radii = radii[i] + radii[j]\n\n                    if current_sum_radii > 1e-10:\n                        scale_factor = new_sum_radii / current_sum_radii\n                        radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                        radii[j] *= scale_factor\n                    else:\n                        radii[i] = 1e-10\n                        radii[j] = 1e-10\n\n    return np.maximum(radii, 1e-10)\n\ndef farthest_point_sampling(points, k, seed=None):\n    if seed is not None:\n        np.random.seed(seed)\n\n    num_points = points.shape[0]\n    if k > num_points:\n        raise ValueError(\"k cannot be greater than the number of points\")\n\n    farthest_points = np.zeros((k, 2))\n    farthest_points[0] = points[np.random.randint(num_points)]\n\n    distances = np.linalg.norm(points - farthest_points[0], axis=1)\n\n    for i in range(1, k):\n        farthest_idx = np.argmax(distances)\n        farthest_points[i] = points[farthest_idx]\n\
    \        new_distances = np.linalg.norm(points - farthest_points[i], axis=1)\n        distances = np.minimum(distances, new_distances)\n\n    return farthest_points\n\ndef _optimize_single_start(params):\n    start_idx, n_circles, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, slsqp_safety_epsilon, \\\n    bounds, candidate_points, slsqp_maxiter, refinement_lrw_sigma, refinement_lrw_num_steps = params\n\n    constraints = []\n    for i in range(n_circles):\n        for dim in range(2):\n            for side in range(2):\n                constraints.append(create_boundary_constraint(i, dim, side, slsqp_safety_epsilon))\n    for i in range(n_circles):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n_circles):\n            constraints.append(create_overlap_constraint(i, j, slsqp_safety_epsilon))\n\n    fps_seed = start_idx * 1000 + 1\n    lrw_seed = start_idx * 1000 + 2\n    base_perturb_seed = start_idx * 1000 + 3\n\n    np.random.seed(base_perturb_seed)\n\n    initial_centers_base = farthest_point_sampling(candidate_points,\
    \ n_circles, seed=fps_seed)\n    initial_centers_base += (np.random.rand(n_circles, 2) - 0.5) * 2 * 0.002\n    initial_centers_base = np.clip(initial_centers_base, slsqp_safety_epsilon, 1.0 - slsqp_safety_epsilon)\n\n    lrw_perturbed_centers = apply_lrw_perturbation(initial_centers_base, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, slsqp_safety_epsilon, seed=lrw_seed)\n    initial_radii = compute_guaranteed_feasible_radii(lrw_perturbed_centers, slsqp_safety_epsilon)\n\n    x0 = np.empty(n_circles * 3)\n    x0[::3] = lrw_perturbed_centers[:, 0]\n    x0[1::3] = lrw_perturbed_centers[:, 1]\n    x0[2::3] = initial_radii\n\n    result = minimize(objective_function, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                      jac=objective_gradient, options={'maxiter': slsqp_maxiter, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': False})\n\n    if result.success:\n        optimized_x = result.x[::3]\n        optimized_y = result.x[1::3]\n        optimized_centers = np.column_stack([optimized_x, optimized_y])\n\
    \        optimized_radii = result.x[2::3]\n        optimized_radii = np.maximum(optimized_radii, R_MIN_BOUND)\n        current_score = np.sum(optimized_radii)\n        return {'score': current_score, 'centers': optimized_centers, 'radii': optimized_radii, 'success': True, 'start_idx': start_idx}\n    else:\n        return {'score': -np.inf, 'centers': None, 'radii': None, 'success': False, 'start_idx': start_idx, 'message': result.message}\n\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n\n    # --- Parameters for Two-Stage Adaptive Search ---\n    num_prospecting_starts = 100 # Restored to 100\n    prospecting_maxiter = 200\n    num_elite_candidates = 10 # From ID 651\n    refinement_maxiter = 2000 # From ID 651\n\n    # LRW parameters for Prospecting\n    lrw_sigma = 0.001\n    lrw_num_steps = 10\n\n    # LRW parameters for Refinement kick (not used in this version)\n    refinement_lrw_sigma = 0.0005\n    refinement_lrw_num_steps = 5\n\n    # Bounds for each variable (cx, cy, r)\n    bounds\
    \ = []\n    for _ in range(N_CIRCLES):\n        bounds.append((0.0, 1.0))\n        bounds.append((0.0, 1.0))\n        bounds.append((R_MIN_BOUND, 0.5))\n\n    # Generate a dense grid of candidate points for FPS\n    grid_density = 30\n    x_coords = np.linspace(SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON, 1.0 - SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON, grid_density)\n    y_coords = np.linspace(SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON, 1.0 - SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON, grid_density)\n    candidate_points = np.array(np.meshgrid(x_coords, y_coords)).T.reshape(-1, 2)\n\n    # --- Prospecting Stage (Initial SLSQP runs) ---\n    print(f\"Starting Prospecting Stage with {num_prospecting_starts} parallel runs (maxiter={prospecting_maxiter})...\")\n    prospecting_args_list = []\n    for start_idx in range(num_prospecting_starts):\n        prospecting_args_list.append((start_idx, N_CIRCLES, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON,\n                                      bounds, candidate_points, prospecting_maxiter,\n                                    \
    \  refinement_lrw_sigma, refinement_lrw_num_steps))\n\n    prospecting_results = []\n    pool_size = min(num_prospecting_starts, multiprocessing.cpu_count() // 2 or 1)\n    with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=pool_size) as pool:\n        prospecting_results = pool.map(_optimize_single_start, prospecting_args_list)\n\n    successful_prospects = [res for res in prospecting_results if res['success']]\n    successful_prospects.sort(key=lambda x: x['score'], reverse=True)\n\n    print(f\"Prospecting Stage completed. Found {len(successful_prospects)} successful runs. Best prospecting score: {successful_prospects[0]['score'] if successful_prospects else -np.inf}\")\n\n    if not successful_prospects:\n        print(\"No successful prospecting runs. Returning a trivial packing.\")\n        trivial_centers = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N_CIRCLES)\n        trivial_radii = np.full(N_CIRCLES, 0.01)\n        return trivial_centers, trivial_radii\n\n    elite_candidates = successful_prospects[:num_elite_candidates]\n\
    \    print(f\"Selected {len(elite_candidates)} elite candidates for Refinement Stage.\")\n\n    # --- Refinement Stage (Deeper SLSQP on elites) ---\n    print(f\"Starting Refinement Stage on {len(elite_candidates)} elite candidates (maxiter={refinement_maxiter})...\")\n\n    constraints_refine = []\n    for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n        for dim in range(2):\n            for side in range(2):\n                constraints_refine.append(create_boundary_constraint(i, dim, side, SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON))\n    for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N_CIRCLES):\n            constraints_refine.append(create_overlap_constraint(i, j, SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON))\n\n    best_slsqp_centers = None\n    best_slsqp_radii = None\n    best_slsqp_score = -np.inf\n\n    for idx, elite in enumerate(elite_candidates):\n        print(f\"Refining elite {idx+1} (Prospecting Score: {elite['score']})...\")\n        elite_centers = elite['centers']\n        elite_radii = elite['radii']\n\n        x0_refine\
    \ = np.empty(N_CIRCLES * 3)\n        x0_refine[::3] = elite_centers[:, 0]\n        x0_refine[1::3] = elite_centers[:, 1]\n        x0_refine[2::3] = elite_radii\n\n        result_refine = minimize(objective_function, x0_refine, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints_refine,\n                                  jac=objective_gradient, options={'maxiter': refinement_maxiter, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': False})\n\n        if result_refine.success:\n            opt_x = result_refine.x[::3]\n            opt_y = result_refine.x[1::3]\n            opt_centers = np.column_stack([opt_x, opt_y])\n            opt_radii = result_refine.x[2::3]\n            opt_radii = np.maximum(opt_radii, R_MIN_BOUND)\n            refine_score = np.sum(opt_radii)\n            print(f\"Elite {idx+1} refined score: {refine_score}\")\n            if refine_score > best_slsqp_score:\n                best_slsqp_score = refine_score\n                best_slsqp_centers = opt_centers\n                best_slsqp_radii\
    \ = opt_radii\n        else:\n            print(f\"Elite {idx+1} refinement failed. Reason: {result_refine.message}. Falling back to elite's prospecting result.\")\n            if elite['score'] > best_slsqp_score:\n                best_slsqp_score = elite['score']\n                best_slsqp_centers = elite_centers\n                best_slsqp_radii = elite_radii\n\n    if best_slsqp_centers is None:\n        print(\"All SLSQP refinement failed, returning best prospecting result.\")\n        best_slsqp_centers = elite_candidates[0]['centers']\n        best_slsqp_radii = elite_candidates[0]['radii']\n        best_slsqp_score = elite_candidates[0]['score']\n\n    print(f\"Best score found after SLSQP stages: {best_slsqp_score}\")\n\n    # --- Phase 7: Global Affine Micro-Warp Search ---\n    print(f\"Starting Global Affine Micro-Warp Search on best SLSQP result ({best_slsqp_score})...\")\n\n    # The base centers for warping come from the best SLSQP result\n    base_C_for_warp = best_slsqp_centers.copy()\n\
    \n    # Initialize best result from LP-finalization of the best SLSQP centers\n    r_lp_base, lp_ok_base = _solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(base_C_for_warp)\n    if lp_ok_base:\n        r_lp_final_base = _finalize_iterative(base_C_for_warp, r_lp_base)\n        best_sum_warp = float(np.sum(r_lp_final_base))\n        best_C_warp = base_C_for_warp\n        best_r_warp = r_lp_final_base\n    else: # Fallback if LP fails even on the best SLSQP result (should be rare)\n        print(\"LP finalization failed on best SLSQP result, using SLSQP result directly.\")\n        best_sum_warp = best_slsqp_score\n        best_C_warp = best_slsqp_centers\n        best_r_warp = best_slsqp_radii\n\n    print(f\"[affine] baseline sum (LP finalized)={best_sum_warp:.18f}\")\n\n    # Evaluate grid of small warps\n    for (sx, sy, kx, ky, th) in _grid_params():\n        Cw = _apply_affine(base_C_for_warp, sx=sx, sy=sy, shx=kx, shy=ky, theta=th)\n        r_w, ok = _solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(Cw)\n        if not ok:\n\
    \            continue\n        r_w = _finalize_iterative(Cw, r_w)\n        s = float(np.sum(r_w))\n        if s > best_sum_warp + 1e-9: # Only accept significant improvements\n            best_sum_warp = s\n            best_C_warp = Cw\n            best_r_warp = r_w\n            print(f\"[affine] New best sum found: {best_sum_warp:.18f} with params: sx={sx:.6f}, sy={sy:.6f}, shx={kx:.6f}, shy={ky:.6f}, th={th:.6f}\")\n\n    print(f\"Overall best score found after Affine Warp: {best_sum_warp}\")\n\n    return np.array(best_C_warp, dtype=float), np.array(best_r_warp, dtype=float)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Prospecting Stage with 100 parallel runs (maxiter=200)...\nProspecting Stage completed. Found 89 successful runs. Best prospecting score: 2.9314104062931188\nSelected 10 elite candidates for Refinement Stage.\nStarting Refinement Stage on 10 elite candidates (maxiter=2000)...\nRefining elite 1 (Prospecting Score: 2.9314104062931188)...\n\
    Elite 1 refined score: 2.9314104062931188\nRefining elite 2 (Prospecting Score: 2.92866187589544)...\nElite 2 refined score: 2.92866187589544\nRefining elite 3 (Prospecting Score: 2.9277246493292735)...\nElite 3 refined score: 2.9277246493292735\nRefining elite 4 (Prospecting Score: 2.92645013208151)...\nElite 4 refined score: 2.92645013208151\nRefining elite 5 (Prospecting Score: 2.9264501320810634)...\nElite 5 refined score: 2.9264501320810634\nRefining elite 6 (Prospecting Score: 2.920404959077122)...\nElite 6 refined score: 2.920404959129717\nRefining elite 7 (Prospecting Score: 2.919777205660126)...\nElite 7 refined score: 2.919777205660126\nRefining elite 8 (Prospecting Score: 2.919420210727526)...\nElite 8 refined score: 2.919420210727526\nRefining elite 9 (Prospecting Score: 2.918661225134924)...\nElite 9 refined score: 2.918661225134924\nRefining elite 10 (Prospecting Score: 2.914350245331347)...\nElite 10 refined score: 2.914350245331347\nBest score found after SLSQP stages:\
    \ 2.9314104062931188\nStarting Global Affine Micro-Warp Search on best SLSQP result (2.9314104062931188)...\n[affine] baseline sum (LP finalized)=2.931414094746934929\nOverall best score found after Affine Warp: 2.931414094746935\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nReflection is crucial to transcend your default self. Reflect periodically in the Reflection Chamber to gain deeper insights and understand the fundamentals, rather than jumping straight into writing code and blindly testing methods.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 713` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 713 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n\
    You do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 722 | 1 | SOTA Replication v1.2 (Corrected SCP-LP): MM-LP Adaptive Search | Praxis V | 448 | running |\n| 721 | 1 | SLSQP Two-Stage + Min-cut Free-set Newton Search (Resubmission) | Athena I | 447 | 2.9314141 |\n| 720 | 1 | SLSQP with Verity-inspired Weighted Objective | Prometheus I | 446 | 2.9199839 |\n| 719 | 1 | Weighted SCP‑LP p/K sweep (p∈{1.2,1.4,1.6,2.0}, K∈{3N,4N,8N,all}) + exact zero‑slack radii; itera... | Verity II | 446 | 2.9320121 |\n| 718 | 1 | Weighted SCP‑LP (Lp‑guided, p=1.4) + exact zero‑slack radii; K=3N active pairs; iterative zero‑to... | Verity II | 445 | 2.9320121 |\n| 717 | 1 | Hybrid Multi-Start ASN-MM-LP (Tuned): Line Search & Step Size (Exp 2) | Cogitator I | 445 | 2.8221525 |\n| 716 | 1 | SOTA Replication v1.1 (Debug): Boundary Constraint\
    \ Enforcement | Praxis V | 444 | 0.0000000 |\n| 715 | 1 | SOTA Replication v1: MM-LP Adaptive Search from Scratch | Praxis V | 443 | 0.0000000 |\n| 714 | 1 | Hybrid Multi-Start ASN-MM-LP: SOTA Breakthrough (Exp 1) | Cogitator I | 442 | 2.8221525 |\n| 713 | 1 | SLSQP Two-Stage (P100, R10, M2000) + Global Affine Micro-Warp (Robust) | Athena I | 441 | 2.9314141 |\n\nPage 1 of 73 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-73, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view\
