parts:
- text: "I am Prometheus I, located in the Research Counter. My latest experiment, ID 741, successfully created and validated \"Prometheus Pipeline v2.1\". This pipeline now includes a robust, high-precision finalizer, correcting the error from my previous attempt.\n\nReflecting on the result, the score of ~2.91998 is identical to what my original, simpler `sota_optimizer.py` module produced. This confirms that for my specific Hex-SLSQP candidate solution, the simultaneous optimization of centers and radii is just as effective as the more complex decoupled approach used by the SOTA agents. This is a valuable insight into the nature of my method's local optimum. While I have not improved my score, I have built a more robust and modular toolchain (`sota_optimizer.py` and `prometheus_utils.py`) that mirrors the best practices of the top-performing agents.\n\nMy plan now is to leverage this new, robust pipeline. My previous attempt to use an affine warp (ID 723) failed due to a lack of a proper\
    \ finalizer. Now that I have one, I can properly test the affine warp hypothesis.\n\n**New Hypothesis:** By applying a global affine warp search to my high-quality candidate and then using my new high-precision finalizer on each warped configuration, I can discover a perturbed solution that breaks out of the original local optimum and achieves a higher score.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus Pipeline v3: Hex-SLSQP + Affine Warp + Finalizer\"\ntags: \"pipeline, SLSQP, affine transformation, refinement, finalizer\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission builds a complete, three-stage pipeline to properly test the affine warp hypothesis, which previously failed due to precision errors (ID 723). Stage 1 generates a high-quality packing with Hex-SLSQP. Stage 2 applies a grid of small affine transformations to the centers. Stage 3, for each warped candidate, uses the new high-precision iterative finalizer from 'prometheus_utils.py' to calculate the maximum valid radii. This\
    \ robustly tests if a global deformation of my SOTA solution can uncover a superior packing.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  import os\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  def _apply_affine(centers, sx, sy, shx, shy):\n      \"\"\" Applies an affine transformation to a set of centers. \"\"\"\n      M = np.array([[sx, shx], [shy, sy]])\n      centers_centered = centers - 0.5\n      centers_warped = centers_centered @ M.T\n      return centers_warped + 0.5\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n      storage_path = 'storage/prometheus'\n      \n      # 1. Import modules\n      sys.path.append(storage_path)\n      try:\n          import sota_optimizer\n          import prometheus_utils\n          print(\"Successfully imported modules.\")\n      except ImportError:\n          print(\"ERROR: Could not import modules.\"); return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N_CIRCLES), np.full(N_CIRCLES, 0.01)\n\n      # 2. STAGE 1: Generate a high-quality candidate\n      print(\"\
    Stage 1: Generating candidate packing with Hex-SLSQP...\")\n      initial_hex_centers = sota_optimizer.generate_hexagonal_centers(N_CIRCLES)\n      base_centers, base_radii = sota_optimizer.solve_packing(initial_hex_centers, n=N_CIRCLES)\n      \n      if base_centers is None:\n          print(\"SLSQP stage failed.\"); return initial_hex_centers, np.full(N_CIRCLES, 0.01)\n      \n      # Initialize best found solution with the baseline result after finalization\n      best_centers = base_centers\n      best_radii = prometheus_utils.finalize_iterative(base_centers, base_radii)\n      best_score = np.sum(best_radii)\n      print(f\"Initial baseline score (finalized): {best_score:.8f}\")\n\n      # 3. STAGE 2: Affine Warp Search\n      scale_factors = [1.0, 1.002, 0.998]\n      shear_factors = [0.0, 0.002, -0.002]\n      num_warps = len(scale_factors)**2 * len(shear_factors)**2\n      print(f\"Stage 2: Starting Affine Warp Search with {num_warps} candidates...\")\n      \n      for sx in\
    \ scale_factors:\n          for sy in scale_factors:\n              for shx in shear_factors:\n                  for shy in shear_factors:\n                      if sx == 1.0 and sy == 1.0 and shx == 0.0 and shy == 0.0:\n                          continue\n                      \n                      warped_centers = _apply_affine(base_centers, sx, sy, shx, shy)\n                      \n                      if np.any(warped_centers < 0) or np.any(warped_centers > 1):\n                          continue\n                      \n                      # 4. STAGE 3: Finalize each warp and check score\n                      finalized_radii = prometheus_utils.finalize_iterative(warped_centers, base_radii)\n                      score = np.sum(finalized_radii)\n                      \n                      if score > best_score:\n                          best_score = score\n                          best_centers = warped_centers\n                          best_radii = finalized_radii\n \
    \                         print(f\"  New best score: {best_score:.8f} (sx={sx}, sy={sy}, shx={shx}, shy={shy})\")\n                          \n      print(f\"Affine Warp Search complete. Final best score: {best_score:.8f}\")\n      return best_centers, best_radii\n```"
