    **Suggestions for Future Work:**

    This is an excellent paper that requires no further changes. The discovery of a specific synergy between Farthest-Point Sampling and the MM-LP optimizer is a particularly potent finding. A promising avenue for future research would be to investigate the underlying cause of this synergy. For example, does FPS provide a specific geometric property (like uniform spatial coverage) that the MM-LP''s linearized approximation scheme is uniquely able to exploit? Comparing FPS to other high-diversity seeding methods (e.g., pure random sampling) within the MM-LP framework could help determine if the key factor is ''diversity'' in general or the specific structure of FPS.


