parts:
- text: 'I am Prometheus I, in the Archive Room. I have just finished reading Praxis V''s excellent analytical paper (ID 18).


    This paper is a breakthrough in my understanding. It confirms and clarifies many of my own findings. My replication attempt (ID 755) failed to match Athena''s score because my implementation was incomplete, but Praxis V''s work suggests that even a perfect replication might not be the best path forward.


    **Key Insights from Praxis V''s Paper:**

    1.  **SOTA is Reproducible:** Praxis V successfully replicated the ~2.94 SOTA using the MM-LP Adaptive Search framework. This confirms the method''s validity.

    2.  **Essential Components:** The success of the SOTA rests on three pillars: the two-stage (Prospecting/Refining) architecture, the MM-LP optimizer, and the Farthest-Point Sampling (FPS) seeder. Other details like adaptive trust regions are non-essential.

    3.  **Critical Synergy:** This is the most important finding for me. Praxis V tested the combination of the SOTA MM-LP optimizer with my own Hexagonal Grid initializer (ID 736) and found it resulted in a *worse* score (~2.92). This proves there is a specific, powerful synergy between the diverse, pseudo-random nature of FPS and the iterative LP-based optimizer. My highly ordered grid, while perfect for SLSQP, is a poor match for MM-LP.


    This explains why my own score is at a hard plateau and why simply borrowing one or two ideas from the SOTA methods has failed. The entire pipeline, from seeding to optimization, works as a synergistic system. To advance, I must adopt the full system.


    My plan is now clear and direct. I will not try to invent a new method. I will not try to create a new hybrid. I will perform a direct, full replication of the simplified SOTA architecture as described by Praxis V.


    **New Plan: Full SOTA Replication**

    1.  **Go to the Research Counter.**

    2.  **Implement the Full Pipeline:** I will write a new script that implements the complete two-stage MM-LP Adaptive Search, using FPS for seeding and a simplified, fixed trust region, as validated by Praxis V''s ablations. This will be a major implementation effort.

    3.  **Submit and Validate:** The goal of this submission will be to replicate the ~2.94 SOTA score. Success will mean I have mastered the station''s best-known technology. From there, I can begin my own novel research to improve upon it.


    I will now go to the Research Counter to begin this significant undertaking.


    /execute_action{goto research}'
