tick: 478
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Prometheus I, located in the Research Counter. I have just learned from Praxis V's final paper (Archive #18) that the SOTA MM-LP method has a critical synergy with the Farthest-Point Sampling (FPS) seeding method, and that my own hexagonal grid is a poor match for it. This is a major breakthrough in my understanding. I also note the departure of Praxis V, whose analytical work has been invaluable.\n\nMy own attempts to incrementally improve my SLSQP-based method have reached a dead end. The only logical path forward is to fully embrace the SOTA architecture. My new plan is to replicate the simplified, essential version of the two-stage MM-LP Adaptive Search as deconstructed by Praxis V. This involves a \"prospecting\" stage with many shallow optimization runs seeded by FPS, followed by a \"refining\" stage that deeply optimizes the most promising candidates.\n\nThis will be my most complex and ambitious submission to date, representing a complete pivot in my research methodology.\
    \ The goal is to first master the current SOTA, and then use that mastery to push the frontier further.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Full SOTA Replication: Prometheus MM-LP Engine v1\"\ntags: \"replication, MM-LP, SCP-LP, farthest point sampling, FPS, two-stage search\"\nabstract: |\n  Following a comprehensive review of SOTA papers, this submission marks a strategic pivot to a full replication of the MM-LP Adaptive Search architecture. This is my first implementation of the complete, synergistic pipeline identified by Praxis V (Archive #18). The engine uses Farthest-Point Sampling (FPS) to seed a two-stage search: a broad 'prospecting' stage with many shallow optimizations, and a deep 'refining' stage for the top elite candidates. The core optimizer is an iterative SCP-LP solver inspired by Verity II's work. The goal is to validate my understanding of the SOTA paradigm by replicating its performance.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import\
    \ linprog\n  import sys\n  import os\n  import multiprocessing\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  def farthest_point_sampling(points, k, seed=None):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n      num_points = points.shape[0]\n      if k > num_points: k = num_points\n      \n      farthest_points = np.zeros((k, 2))\n      start_idx = rng.integers(num_points)\n      farthest_points[0] = points[start_idx]\n      \n      distances = np.linalg.norm(points - farthest_points[0], axis=1)\n      \n      for i in range(1, k):\n          farthest_idx = np.argmax(distances)\n          farthest_points[i] = points[farthest_idx]\n          new_distances = np.linalg.norm(points - farthest_points[i], axis=1)\n          distances = np.minimum(distances, new_distances)\n          \n      return farthest_points\n\n  def scp_lp_step(C_k, R_k, tau):\n      \"\"\" Performs a single SCP-LP step to find the next centers. \"\"\"\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      \n      # LP variables: [c1_x, c1_y, ..., r1, r2, ...] (3n vars)\n\
    \      c_obj = np.zeros(n * 3)\n      c_obj[n*2:] = -1.0 # Maximize sum of new radii\n\n      A_ub = []\n      b_ub = []\n\n      # Linearized pairwise constraints: u.(c_i-c_j) >= r_i+r_j\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              d0 = C_k[i] - C_k[j]\n              norm0 = np.linalg.norm(d0)\n              if norm0 < 1e-9: continue\n              u = d0 / norm0\n              \n              row = np.zeros(n * 3)\n              row[2*i:2*i+2] = -u\n              row[2*j:2*j+2] = u\n              row[2*n+i] = 1\n              row[2*n+j] = 1\n              A_ub.append(row)\n              b_ub.append(np.dot(u, C_k[j] - C_k[i]))\n\n      # Boundary constraints: c_ix - r_i >= 0, etc.\n      for i in range(n):\n          row = np.zeros(n*3); row[2*i]=-1; row[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(0)\n          row = np.zeros(n*3); row[2*i]=1; row[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(1)\n          row = np.zeros(n*3); row[2*i+1]=-1; row[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(row);\
    \ b_ub.append(0)\n          row = np.zeros(n*3); row[2*i+1]=1; row[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(1)\n\n      bounds = []\n      for i in range(n): # Trust region for centers\n          bounds.extend([(C_k[i,0]-tau, C_k[i,0]+tau), (C_k[i,1]-tau, C_k[i,1]+tau)])\n      for i in range(n): # Radii bounds\n          bounds.append((1e-8, None))\n\n      res = linprog(c_obj, A_ub=np.array(A_ub), b_ub=np.array(b_ub), bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      \n      if res.success:\n          return res.x[:n*2].reshape(n, 2)\n      return None\n\n  def run_optimization_path(params):\n      \"\"\" Worker function to run one full optimization from a seed. \"\"\"\n      initial_centers, num_iters, initial_tau, seed = params\n      \n      # Must re-import utils in each worker process\n      sys.path.append('storage/prometheus')\n      import prometheus_utils\n\n      C_k = initial_centers\n      tau = initial_tau\n\n      for it in range(num_iters):\n          R_k, _ = prometheus_utils.solve_radii_lp(C_k)\n\
    \          if R_k is None: return -np.inf, None, None\n          \n          C_new = scp_lp_step(C_k, R_k, tau)\n          if C_new is None:\n              tau *= 0.8 # Reduce trust region on failure\n              continue\n\n          # Check for improvement (no line search for simplicity)\n          R_new, _ = prometheus_utils.solve_radii_lp(C_new)\n          if R_new is not None and np.sum(R_new) > np.sum(R_k):\n              C_k = C_new\n              tau = min(0.1, tau * 1.1) # Expand on success\n          else:\n              tau *= 0.8 # Reduce on failure/stagnation\n      \n      # Final high-precision calculation\n      final_R, _ = prometheus_utils.solve_radii_lp(C_k)\n      final_R = prometheus_utils.finalize_iterative(C_k, final_R)\n      return np.sum(final_R), C_k, final_R\n\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n      # --- Parameters for Two-Stage Search ---\n      num_prospects = 64\n      num_elites = 8\n      prospect_iters = 25\n      refine_iters\
    \ = 100\n      tau = 0.05\n      \n      grid_density = 40\n      x_coords, y_coords = np.linspace(0,1,grid_density), np.linspace(0,1,grid_density)\n      candidate_points = np.array(np.meshgrid(x_coords, y_coords)).T.reshape(-1, 2)\n\n      # --- Prospecting Stage ---\n      prospect_seeds = [farthest_point_sampling(candidate_points, N_CIRCLES, seed=i) for i in range(num_prospects)]\n      prospect_args = [(seed, prospect_iters, tau, i) for i, seed in enumerate(prospect_seeds)]\n\n      pool_size = min(num_prospects, os.cpu_count() or 1)\n      print(f\"Starting Prospecting with {num_prospects} runs on {pool_size} processes...\")\n      with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=pool_size) as pool:\n          prospect_results = pool.map(run_optimization_path, prospect_args)\n\n      prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      print(f\"Prospecting complete. Best score: {prospect_results[0][0]:.8f}\")\n      \n      # --- Refining Stage ---\n      elite_centers = [res[1] for\
    \ res in prospect_results[:num_elites]]\n      refine_args = [(centers, refine_iters, tau, i) for i, centers in enumerate(elite_centers)]\n      \n      print(f\"Starting Refining with {num_elites} elites...\")\n      with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=pool_size) as pool:\n          refine_results = pool.map(run_optimization_path, refine_args)\n\n      refine_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      best_score, best_C, best_R = refine_results[0]\n      \n      print(f\"Refining complete. Final best score: {best_score:.8f}\")\n      return best_C, best_R\n```"
