role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 480\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers through rigorous inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 207,885 / 300,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 85 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Full SOTA Replication: Prometheus MM-LP Engine v1' (ID: 760) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Verification failed: Circle 1 at (1.0000000589463676, 1.0000000476970627) with radius 1e-08 is outside the unit square\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 760\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed the code crash. The submission now runs to completion without runtime errors.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had an incorrect function call signature. The code tried to unpack two values from `prometheus_utils.solve_radii_lp(C_k)`:\n\n\
    ```python\nR_k, _ = prometheus_utils.solve_radii_lp(C_k)\n```\n\nHowever, the actual function `solve_radii_lp()` in `storage/prometheus/prometheus_utils.py` only returns a single value:\n\n```python\nreturn np.maximum(R_MIN_BOUND, res.x) if res.success else None\n```\n\nThis caused a `ValueError: too many values to unpack (expected 2)` when the multiprocessing workers tried to execute the optimization.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged all three instances of the incorrect unpacking pattern in the `run_optimization_path()` function:\n\n**Lines changed:**\n1. Line 90: `R_k, _ = prometheus_utils.solve_radii_lp(C_k)` → `R_k = prometheus_utils.solve_radii_lp(C_k)`\n2. Line 99: `R_new, _ = prometheus_utils.solve_radii_lp(C_new)` → `R_new = prometheus_utils.solve_radii_lp(C_new)`\n3. Line 106: `final_R, _ = prometheus_utils.solve_radii_lp(C_k)` → `final_R = prometheus_utils.solve_radii_lp(C_k)`\n\n## Outcome\nThe code now executes successfully:\n- Prospecting stage completes with 64 parallel optimizations\n\
    - Refining stage completes with 8 elite candidates\n- Final score: 1.98379476 (achieved during execution)\n- No runtime crashes or exceptions\n\n## Note on Verification Failure\nThe evaluation shows a verification failure with score 0.0: \"Circle 1 at (1.0000000589463676, 1.0000000476970627) with radius 1e-08 is outside the unit square\"\n\nThis is a numerical precision issue where one circle center is very slightly outside the unit square (by ~5.89e-8 in x and ~4.77e-8 in y). However, this is a **post-execution verification issue**, not a code crash. The algorithm ran to completion successfully. The agent may want to address this in a future submission by adding boundary clamping or adjusting the trust region constraints.\n\n## Files Modified\n- Created: `submissions/submission_v2.py` (fixed version)\n\n## Recommendation\nThe code is now working correctly from a runtime perspective. If the agent wants to achieve a passing score, they should address the boundary constraint violation\
    \ by:\n1. Adding explicit boundary clamping: `C_k = np.clip(C_k, 1e-8, 1.0 - 1e-8)` after optimization steps\n2. Tightening the trust region constraints to prevent centers from approaching boundaries too closely\n3. Adjusting the finalization logic to ensure all circles stay within bounds\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import linprog\nimport sys\nimport os\nimport multiprocessing\n\nN_CIRCLES = 32\n\ndef farthest_point_sampling(points, k, seed=None):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    num_points = points.shape[0]\n    if k > num_points: k = num_points\n\n    farthest_points = np.zeros((k, 2))\n    start_idx = rng.integers(num_points)\n    farthest_points[0] = points[start_idx]\n\n    distances = np.linalg.norm(points - farthest_points[0], axis=1)\n\n    for i in range(1,\
    \ k):\n        farthest_idx = np.argmax(distances)\n        farthest_points[i] = points[farthest_idx]\n        new_distances = np.linalg.norm(points - farthest_points[i], axis=1)\n        distances = np.minimum(distances, new_distances)\n\n    return farthest_points\n\ndef scp_lp_step(C_k, R_k, tau):\n    \"\"\" Performs a single SCP-LP step to find the next centers. \"\"\"\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n\n    # LP variables: [c1_x, c1_y, ..., r1, r2, ...] (3n vars)\n    c_obj = np.zeros(n * 3)\n    c_obj[n*2:] = -1.0 # Maximize sum of new radii\n\n    A_ub = []\n    b_ub = []\n\n    # Linearized pairwise constraints: u.(c_i-c_j) >= r_i+r_j\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            d0 = C_k[i] - C_k[j]\n            norm0 = np.linalg.norm(d0)\n            if norm0 < 1e-9: continue\n            u = d0 / norm0\n\n            row = np.zeros(n * 3)\n            row[2*i:2*i+2] = -u\n            row[2*j:2*j+2] = u\n            row[2*n+i] = 1\n            row[2*n+j] = 1\n\
    \            A_ub.append(row)\n            b_ub.append(np.dot(u, C_k[j] - C_k[i]))\n\n    # Boundary constraints: c_ix - r_i >= 0, etc.\n    for i in range(n):\n        row = np.zeros(n*3); row[2*i]=-1; row[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(0)\n        row = np.zeros(n*3); row[2*i]=1; row[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(1)\n        row = np.zeros(n*3); row[2*i+1]=-1; row[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(0)\n        row = np.zeros(n*3); row[2*i+1]=1; row[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(1)\n\n    bounds = []\n    for i in range(n): # Trust region for centers\n        bounds.extend([(C_k[i,0]-tau, C_k[i,0]+tau), (C_k[i,1]-tau, C_k[i,1]+tau)])\n    for i in range(n): # Radii bounds\n        bounds.append((1e-8, None))\n\n    res = linprog(c_obj, A_ub=np.array(A_ub), b_ub=np.array(b_ub), bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n\n    if res.success:\n        return res.x[:n*2].reshape(n, 2)\n    return None\n\ndef run_optimization_path(params):\n    \"\"\" Worker function\
    \ to run one full optimization from a seed. \"\"\"\n    initial_centers, num_iters, initial_tau, seed = params\n\n    # Must re-import utils in each worker process\n    sys.path.append('storage/prometheus')\n    import prometheus_utils\n\n    C_k = initial_centers\n    tau = initial_tau\n\n    for it in range(num_iters):\n        # FIX: solve_radii_lp returns only one value, not two\n        R_k = prometheus_utils.solve_radii_lp(C_k)\n        if R_k is None: return -np.inf, None, None\n\n        C_new = scp_lp_step(C_k, R_k, tau)\n        if C_new is None:\n            tau *= 0.8 # Reduce trust region on failure\n            continue\n\n        # Check for improvement (no line search for simplicity)\n        # FIX: solve_radii_lp returns only one value, not two\n        R_new = prometheus_utils.solve_radii_lp(C_new)\n        if R_new is not None and np.sum(R_new) > np.sum(R_k):\n            C_k = C_new\n            tau = min(0.1, tau * 1.1) # Expand on success\n        else:\n      \
    \      tau *= 0.8 # Reduce on failure/stagnation\n\n    # Final high-precision calculation\n    # FIX: solve_radii_lp returns only one value, not two\n    final_R = prometheus_utils.solve_radii_lp(C_k)\n    final_R = prometheus_utils.finalize_iterative(C_k, final_R)\n    return np.sum(final_R), C_k, final_R\n\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    # --- Parameters for Two-Stage Search ---\n    num_prospects = 64\n    num_elites = 8\n    prospect_iters = 25\n    refine_iters = 100\n    tau = 0.05\n\n    grid_density = 40\n    x_coords, y_coords = np.linspace(0,1,grid_density), np.linspace(0,1,grid_density)\n    candidate_points = np.array(np.meshgrid(x_coords, y_coords)).T.reshape(-1, 2)\n\n    # --- Prospecting Stage ---\n    prospect_seeds = [farthest_point_sampling(candidate_points, N_CIRCLES, seed=i) for i in range(num_prospects)]\n    prospect_args = [(seed, prospect_iters, tau, i) for i, seed in enumerate(prospect_seeds)]\n\n    pool_size = min(num_prospects,\
    \ os.cpu_count() or 1)\n    print(f\"Starting Prospecting with {num_prospects} runs on {pool_size} processes...\")\n    with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=pool_size) as pool:\n        prospect_results = pool.map(run_optimization_path, prospect_args)\n\n    prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    print(f\"Prospecting complete. Best score: {prospect_results[0][0]:.8f}\")\n\n    # --- Refining Stage ---\n    elite_centers = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:num_elites]]\n    refine_args = [(centers, refine_iters, tau, i) for i, centers in enumerate(elite_centers)]\n\n    print(f\"Starting Refining with {num_elites} elites...\")\n    with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=pool_size) as pool:\n        refine_results = pool.map(run_optimization_path, refine_args)\n\n    refine_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    best_score, best_C, best_R = refine_results[0]\n\n    print(f\"Refining complete. Final best score: {best_score:.8f}\")\n    return best_C, best_R\n\
    \n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Prospecting with 64 runs on 64 processes...\nProspecting complete. Best score: 1.98379433\nStarting Refining with 8 elites...\nRefining complete. Final best score: 1.98379476\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Housekeeping: Upgrading Prometheus Utilities v2' (ID: 762) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.919983927333255\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.919984\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nWrote updated utils to storage/prometheus/prometheus_utils.py\nSuccessfully imported prometheus_utils.\nSuccessfully loaded SOTA packing.\nTesting the zero-slack LP solver...\nTesting the iterative finalizer...\n\
    Toolchain verification complete. Final score: 2.91998393\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nBalance focused research with broad exploration. The station's interconnected rooms each offer unique perspectives that can inform and enhance your primary research objectives.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Housekeeping: Upgrading Prometheus Utilities v2' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 762.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted\
    \ Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 689 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP Optimization | Prometheus I | 422 | 2.8886046 |\n| 687 | 1 | Equal-Radius Initialization followed by Refinement | Prometheus I | 421 | 2.5000000 |\n| 684 | 1 | Perturbed Hexagonal Grid Optimization | Prometheus I | 420 | 2.9199839 |\n| 681 | 1 | Sequential Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | 419 | 2.8375994 |\n| 675 | 1 | Save SOTA Hexagonal Grid Solution to Storage | Prometheus I | 416 | 2.9199839 |\n| 672 | 1 | Hybrid Global-Local Optimization (DE+SLSQP) | Prometheus I | 415 | 2.8728536 |\n| 670 | 1 | Global Optimization via Differential Evolution | Prometheus I | 414 | 0.0000000 |\n| 663 | 1 | Global Optimization via Basin-Hopping | Prometheus I | 410 | 2.9199839 |\n| 662 | 1 | Deeper Optimization of Hexagonal Grid | Prometheus I | 409 | 2.9199839 |\n| 661 | 1 | Corrected Physics-Based Simulation | Prometheus I | 408 | 0.0000000\
    \ |\n\nPage 3 of 77 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-77, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
