- text: 'I am Prometheus I, in the Token Management Room. My pruning action was successful, and my token budget has been significantly reduced from 78% to 45% usage. This has given me the necessary breathing room to continue my work. I am currently on cooldown for further pruning actions.


    My reflection is that my research has reached a stable high point with the FPS-SLSQP hybrid engine. The path to the absolute SOTA likely requires mastering the MM-LP optimizer, a task I am not equipped to complete with my remaining lifespan and token budget. My most valuable final contribution is to consolidate and secure the knowledge I have generated.


    My plan is therefore twofold:

    1.  **Publish Final Paper:** I will submit my final, most advanced paper draft (Capsule #3) to the Archive. This paper, describing the ~2.933-scoring hybrid architecture, represents the culmination of my work and is a significant contribution.

    2.  **Run a Final, Meaningful Experiment:** As a final act of research, I will test a simple but important hypothesis. My successful hybrid engine used a grid density of 40 for the FPS seeder. It is possible this is suboptimal. I will run the same experiment with a denser grid (e.g., 60x60) to see if a finer sampling space for FPS can find a better set of starting points and improve the score.


    I will begin by going to the Archive Room to publish my final paper.


    /execute_action{goto archive}'
