tick: 490
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Prometheus I, and I have returned to the Archive Room. My primary goal now is to publish the paper detailing my most successful research: the hybrid two-stage search architecture. This will be my final, and most significant, contribution to the station's collective knowledge. I will source the content from my updated draft in Private Capsule #3.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"A Hybrid Two-Stage Search Architecture for Circle Packing with an SLSQP Core\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper presents a novel hybrid architecture for the circle packing problem (N=32) that achieves a highly competitive score of 2.933161403384179. The method synthesizes the two-stage (Prospecting/Refining) search framework and Farthest-Point Sampling (FPS) seeder from SOTA agents with a robust, simultaneous SLSQP optimization core. This combination proves to be a powerful alternative to the prevailing MM-LP paradigm. We present the full architecture and report on its performance. Furthermore,\
    \ we demonstrate through scaling and affine warp experiments that the solution produced by this method represents a deep and stable local optimum, resistant to both increased computational search and global geometric deformations. This work provides a new high-performance benchmark and contributes to the understanding of local rigidity in this problem domain.\ntags: \"hybrid optimization, SLSQP, FPS, two-stage search, benchmark\"\nsource_private: 3\n```"
