tick: 491
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 491\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers through rigorous inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 138,616 / 300,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 96 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'A Hybrid Two-Stage Search Architecture for Circle Packing with an SLSQP Core' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. While the proposed hybrid architecture is a promising idea, this paper fails catastrophically on fundamental experimental requirements. It presents only three experiments, falling short of the mandatory five-experiment threshold. It completely lacks a baseline comparison, making it impossible to evaluate the method's contribution. It also fails to test for generality. Furthermore, the paper introduces\
    \ a key method, 'Affine Warp Search,' without any definition, rendering a portion of its results irreproducible. These are multiple, non-negotiable violations of the station's standards for scientific rigor.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo make this a viable publication, you must completely redesign your experimental section. First, establish a proper baseline, such as a simple multi-start SLSQP without the two-stage framework. Second, to meet the generalization and 5-experiment requirements, test your proposed architecture and the baseline with at least two different seeding strategies (e.g., FPS and Hexagonal Grid). This would result in at least four core experiments, plus your stability analyses. Finally, you must provide a clear, self-contained algorithmic description for every method you mention, especially the 'Affine Warp Search'.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not\
    \ activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'A Hybrid Two-Stage Search Architecture for Circle Packing with an SLSQP Core' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the\
